#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078358 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "06d5e05a-4595-551f-8c1b-7c585f69b47b" :question/math-academy-id "e-74" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} }.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & =\\frac{4-2\\sqrt{4}}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {(x -2 \\sqrt{x})(x+2\\sqrt x)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n            &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-\\left(2\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-4x} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x(x-4)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x} {x+2\\sqrt x} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {4} {4+2\\sqrt4} \\\n\t    &=\\dfrac 1 2.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078359 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "7db311cd-70a0-50f4-8984-4a578abc67eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-75" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x +1} -1}  }.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} \n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(3x)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\left(\\sqrt{x+1}\\right)^2-1^2}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x+1-1}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}3(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)\\\n&=3(\\sqrt{0+1}+1)\\\n\t&=6.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02ecad5c-e584-50db-88c3-15299c26bf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235814} {:answer/id #uuid "1f989bd7-1f94-5c18-a307-0e14bf920698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236018} {:answer/id #uuid "29070754-7715-55c3-b391-6bbcceecf31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236075} {:answer/id #uuid "d6baaf9f-3cb0-56ab-8c42-72e4721ed87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237176} {:answer/id #uuid "e5d7caa8-9193-5bd5-a2f0-dba99b5af8ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6baaf9f-3cb0-56ab-8c42-72e4721ed87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237176} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50d008a-d262-500c-9ca0-4f2f20947840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6df53e19-d535-55b0-b903-86ff970515ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-101288" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=2$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x+1-7} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3(x-2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2748da3d-de9c-588f-a272-4477627a5871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241519} {:answer/id #uuid "436f6a8a-0012-536a-8240-8aceafb979a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241787} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc51a6c-869f-5dfb-8a5a-c88113a1c338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3+\\sqrt{8}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242154} {:answer/id #uuid "83b57267-3074-53f8-b55c-0ecee3de87c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242333} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4814af-1e6f-5652-918c-6984a5ec7ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{8}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83b57267-3074-53f8-b55c-0ecee3de87c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242333} :answer-field/id #uuid "062033bc-5981-57ac-b024-99d02652d9cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "178aeb65-207a-5b33-817e-06f448b4747e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107061" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{3x-1}-\\sqrt{8}}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=3$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{3x-1}-\\sqrt{8}} & =\\frac{3-3}{\\sqrt{3(3)-1}-\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3}{\\sqrt{8}-\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{3x-1}-\\sqrt{8}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8})}{(\\sqrt{3x-1}-\\sqrt{8})(\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8})}{(\\sqrt{3x-1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8})}{3x-1-8} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8})}{3(x-3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{3x-1}+\\sqrt{8}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(3)-1}+\\sqrt{8}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}+\\sqrt{8}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{8}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e713aa29-49dc-5774-8f3d-14d36ee8df02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e713aa29-49dc-5774-8f3d-14d36ee8df02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570527} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d8564e2-8428-52a2-bc1e-e897b6b73c0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "782d71a6-13dd-5aa9-bf77-a0e9f83d71b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-338468" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}-1}{1-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)}{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{1}^{2}}{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\cancel{x-1}}{\\cancel{(x-1)}(\\sqrt{x}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80047bfb-3e47-5e41-8b5c-6ac44778168d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80047bfb-3e47-5e41-8b5c-6ac44778168d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309752} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca979b3-26b5-587f-8ed2-78b1175b6e43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6781a2e-1ec2-5731-b57e-58bd3e75cec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-338484" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}{{3}^{2}-3-6}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{({x}^{2}-x-6)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x+1)-4}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3+2)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9067c7d-48d8-5e12-8a8e-bdb652ef0dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9067c7d-48d8-5e12-8a8e-bdb652ef0dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570531} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec686454-e333-5ef0-819d-3784c306b3b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b9cc1bf-d4a8-55a1-963a-af1d9f3db029" :question/math-academy-id "q-338485" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3x+25}}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3x+25}}{x} & =\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3(0)+25}}{0}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3x+25}}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(5-\\sqrt{3x+25})(5+\\sqrt{3x+25})}{x(5+\\sqrt{3x+25})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{5}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{3x+25})}^{2}}{x(5+\\sqrt{3x+25})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{25-(3x+25)}{x(5+\\sqrt{3x+25})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-3x}{x(5+\\sqrt{3x+25})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-3}{5+\\sqrt{3x+25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{5+\\sqrt{3(0)+25}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e07e547-aa89-5cae-8d95-54625e3c375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e07e547-aa89-5cae-8d95-54625e3c375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570347} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad2d4819-5891-5f49-ae40-2b183406271e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "386a05f8-a2c4-54b1-8442-7cec1d9c62b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-338523" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{3x+2}-\\sqrt{4x+1}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=1,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{3x+2}-\\sqrt{4x+1}} & =\\frac{1-1}{\\sqrt{3(1)+2}-\\sqrt{4(1)+1}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{3x+2}-\\sqrt{4x+1}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})}{(\\sqrt{3x+2}-\\sqrt{4x+1})(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})}{(\\sqrt{3x+2})^{2}-(\\sqrt{4x+1})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})}{(3x+2)-(4x+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-(1-x)(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})}{1-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}[-(\\sqrt{3x+2}+\\sqrt{4x+1})] \\\\  & =-(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b612a4f-e1c6-5914-9b1c-cd76d08b8654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327737} {:answer/id #uuid "8986b242-cabf-515e-8d37-532d5c40fea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328118} {:answer/id #uuid "b378ea97-a8d4-5e8e-9d2d-1c1b3bcc45e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328493} {:answer/id #uuid "b4973e3a-e428-5a76-8538-7eda97adaaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328504} {:answer/id #uuid "c22d4859-8b9b-5ead-9262-87aad15210b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4973e3a-e428-5a76-8538-7eda97adaaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328504} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7a419a-a6d4-58fb-8ef0-cea5378f18c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac424d04-f294-52bc-866a-9d33ace21adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-4467" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+5}-\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{(\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5})(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{{(\\sqrt{x+5})}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x+5-5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+5}+\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d1c6da9-f3e0-545e-99b7-211c6ba45633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570316} {:answer/id #uuid "ae65fcbc-3006-5c14-89e6-8ebed74524ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570438} {:answer/id #uuid "b179e100-1a56-51bc-9676-7dda7eb65e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570446} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4c2b31-de7b-5189-866e-8f0ddf3316c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570479} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8608e-e15b-5350-9981-cd57b649d33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b179e100-1a56-51bc-9676-7dda7eb65e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570446} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a13345-7a00-5a93-b9a2-544eb1b7c369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13cd01f5-b70e-51c8-add8-d0b755916801" :question/math-academy-id "q-46832" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{8-4\\sqrt{x}}{x-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{8-4\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & =\\frac{8-4\\sqrt{4}}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{8-4\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{4(2-\\sqrt{x})}{x-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{4(2-\\sqrt{x})(2+\\sqrt{x})}{(x-4)(2+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{4({2}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2})}{(x-4)(2+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{4(4-x)}{(x-4)(2+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{-4(x-4)}{(x-4)(2+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\frac{-4}{2+\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2+\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b03e9b7-6868-53d3-a895-8e4fdbdf9bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570142} {:answer/id #uuid "22efaf2d-5390-5601-8a1b-287b90036eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570187} {:answer/id #uuid "7480c9f6-e405-5332-a8c3-73853a075b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570334} {:answer/id #uuid "99493345-01cb-5276-9363-0b8dd99f66ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570396} {:answer/id #uuid "a026f1d8-6c30-50f1-91a2-41e1f6bd150f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7480c9f6-e405-5332-a8c3-73853a075b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570334} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c38e3c1-1d1c-5a27-b17b-40b29b8fb328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "662345c5-cd55-5265-8f67-e438e3ccf7b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-46837" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3x}}{x-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3x}}{x-3} & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3(3)}}{3-3}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3x}}{x-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{(3-\\sqrt{3x})(3+\\sqrt{3x})}{(x-3)(3+\\sqrt{3x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{{3}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{3x})}^{2}}{(x-3)(3+\\sqrt{3x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{9-3x}{(x-3)(3+\\sqrt{3x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{-3(x-3)}{(x-3)(3+\\sqrt{3x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{-3}{3+\\sqrt{3x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3+\\sqrt{3\\cdot 3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8836b938-9934-5409-9f10-b4cd7ecd94f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076497} {:answer/id #uuid "8b54c412-bad4-597e-8f0a-6225d88f3773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076498} {:answer/id #uuid "9e409971-c2d3-5b6e-82ee-3468d654e307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076499} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a5d0a3-5345-59e8-a53d-391d532ea4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076500} {:answer/id #uuid "53a20335-f8bf-5362-b368-968fcc33eef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076501}] :answer-field/id #uuid "351ba727-ee60-5614-b40f-f04d04640276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "275aca41-deff-5886-80e8-6744866e7e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-46840" :question/problem "Evaluate $lim_(x → 1^{+})\\frac{1 - x^{2}}{1 - \\sqrt{x}}$."}]}
